{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'vibe --help'","aggregated_output":"Run the Mistral Vibe interactive CLI\n\nUsage: vibe [OPTIONS] [INITIAL_PROMPT] [COMMAND]\n\nCommands:\n  mcp     Manage MCP server configuration without starting a session\n  config  Describe Vibe's configuration without starting a session\n  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nArguments:\n  [INITIAL_PROMPT]  Initial prompt for the interactive session, or the prompt in headless mode\n\nOptions:\n  -v, --version\n          Show version and exit\n      --workdir <CWD>\n          Change to this directory before running [env: VIBE_CWD=]\n  -c, --continue\n          Continue this terminal's last session in this folder, else the folder's most recent\n      --resume [<RESUME>]\n          Resume a session. Without SESSION_ID, shows an interactive picker\n      --setup\n          Setup API key and exit\n  -p, --prompt [<PROMPT>]\n          Run in headless (programmatic) mode: send prompt, output response, exit\n      --output <OUTPUT>\n          Output format for headless mode [default: text] [possible values: text, json, streaming]\n      --max-turns <MAX_TURNS>\n          Maximum number of assistant turns (headless mode only)\n      --max-price <MAX_PRICE>\n          Maximum cost in dollars (headless mode only)\n      --max-tokens <MAX_TOKENS>\n          Maximum total prompt + completion tokens (headless mode only)\n      --time-limit <SECONDS>\n          Interrupt the run once SECONDS have passed since start, write the export and exit 3. SIGTERM stops the run the same way\n      --prompt-file <PATH>\n          Run in programmatic mode with the prompt read from PATH, instead of -p TEXT or stdin\n      --system-prompt-file <PATH>\n          Replace Vibe's own system prompt instructions with the text in PATH (headless mode only). Project context and AGENTS.md still follow it\n      --output-dir <DIR>\n          On every exit, write export.json (Vibe version, effective config, token usage, cost, stop reason, outcome) and a copy of the session journal (session/) to DIR\n      --agent <NAME>\n          Agent to use (builtin: ask, accept-edits, smart-approve, auto-approve, or custom from ~/.vibe/agents/NAME.toml). Defaults to the 'default_agent' config setting\n      --model <ALIAS>\n          Model alias to use instead of 'active_model' (headless mode only, new sessions). Not saved as the default\n      --auto-approve\n          Approves all tool calls without prompting for the selected agent [alias: --yolo]\n      --smart-approve\n          Classify each tool call and auto-run the safe ones, prompting only for risky ones\n      --enabled-tools <ENABLED_TOOLS>\n          Enable specific tools (headless: disables all others). Repeat the flag\n      --disabled-tools <DISABLED_TOOLS>\n          Disable specific tools after --enabled-tools filtering. Repeat the flag\n      --trust\n          Trust the working directory for this invocation only\n      --worktree [<WORKTREE>]\n          Run inside a git worktree under $VIBE_HOME/worktrees. With NAME, create (or reuse) a worktree and branch named NAME. Without NAME, create a new one named after the prompt (or a random slug). Combines with `-c`/`--resume`: the worktree is prepared first and the resume is then scoped to the worktree directory\n      --add-dir <ADD_DIR>\n          Additional working directory for file access. Repeat the flag\n      --check-upgrade\n          Check for a Vibe update now, prompt to install it, and exit\n  -h, --help\n          Print help\n\nCommands:\n  update         Check for a Vibe update now (same as --check-upgrade).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
