{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'bash -n run-vibe.sh && git diff --check && git diff -- run-vibe.sh && cat ANSWER.md && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/run-vibe.sh b/run-vibe.sh\nindex c4a5223..efff9cb 100755\n--- a/run-vibe.sh\n+++ b/run-vibe.sh\n@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ SH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/vhome-XXXXXX); VH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/vibehome-XXXXXX)\n cp \"$D/vibe/config.toml\" \"$VH/config.toml\"\n mkdir -p \"$D/logs\"\n ( cd \"$W\" && env -i PATH=\"$PATH\" TERM=\"${TERM:-dumb}\" LANG=\"${LANG:-en_US.UTF-8}\" HOME=\"$SH\" VIBE_HOME=\"$VH\" \\\n-    OPENROUTER_API_KEY=\"$OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\n+    OPENROUTER_API_KEY=\"$OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" MISTRAL_API_KEY=unused-placeholder \\\n     sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/agent.sb\" \\\n     \"$VIBE\" -p \"$PROMPT\" --model devstral --auto-approve --trust --output streaming --output-dir \"$VH/out\" \\\n       --max-price 1.5 --time-limit 1200 < /dev/null > \"$D/logs/last-run.out\" 2> \"$D/logs/last-run.err\" )\n# Cause\n\nVibe 3.1.0 checks for `MISTRAL_API_KEY` during startup even when the configured model uses OpenRouter. The launcher's `env -i` removed that variable, so Vibe tried to read API keys from the macOS Keychain via `/usr/bin/security`. `agent.sb` correctly blocks that command, causing the immediate exit 2 before any run or export.\n\nThe launcher now supplies an inert `MISTRAL_API_KEY` placeholder to prevent the Keychain lookup. The OpenRouter provider still uses `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`; the real key is not copied to the Mistral variable. The sandbox's Keychain denial remains in place.\n M run-vibe.sh\n?? ANSWER.md\n?? vibe/logs/\n?? vibe/trusted_folders.toml\n?? vibe/vibehistory\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
